-- title:
--   Vélu's μ₂-isogeny sends toric point c to c²
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $m$ a nonzero natural number. Write $W_m$ for the Tate curve $(1,0,0,\mathrm{tateA4},\mathrm{tateA6})$ over $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$, obtained from `tatePowerSeries` over $\mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ by coefficient extension and then base-changed along the ring homomorphism `qExpand K m`, which multiplies all exponents by $m$ (so $q \mapsto q^m$). Let $C = (u,r,s,t)$ be a Weierstrass variable change over $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ with $u = 2$, $r = 1/4$, $s = 1/2$ and $t = -1/8$ as constant Hahn series, and let $c \in K$ satisfy $c \neq 0$ and $c^2 \neq 1$. Put $(x_0,y_0) = \mathrm{toricPoint}\,K\,m\,(-1)$ and $(x,y) = \mathrm{toricPoint}\,K\,m\,c$, the explicit Laurent series $X(u,q^m), Y(u,q^m)$ of Tate's uniformisation at $u = -1$ and $u = c$, and set $g = 3x_0^2 + 2 (W_m.a_2) x_0 + W_m.a_4 - (W_m.a_1) y_0$. Then the two coordinates
--   $$\Bigl(u^{-2}\bigl(x + \tfrac{g}{x-x_0} - r\bigr),\quad u^{-3}\bigl(y - \tfrac{g\,(a_1(x-x_0) + y - y_0)}{(x-x_0)^2} - t - s\bigl(x + \tfrac{g}{x-x_0} - r\bigr)\bigr)\Bigr)$$
--   are equal, respectively, to the first and second components of $\mathrm{toricPoint}\,K\,(m\cdot 2)\,(c^2)$.
--
--   This is the point half of the degree-two step $E_{q^m}/\mu_2 \cong E_{q^{2m}}$ for Tate curves: after the normalising substitution $C$, Vélu's isogeny with kernel generated by the toric $2$-torsion point $u = -1$ acts as $u \mapsto u^2$ on Tate's uniformisation, the target being the Tate curve of $q^{2m}$. It is used, together with the companion identification of the quotient curve, in [`ModularCurve.variableChange_veluQuotient2_tateLaurent_cyclotomicUniv_eq_and_vcXInvR_velu2XR_tateToricPoint_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.variableChange_veluQuotient2_tateLaurent_cyclotomicUniv_eq_and_vcXInvR_velu2XR_tateToricPoint_eq), a step towards the computation of $j$ of the quotients $E_q/\mu_d$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_vcXInv_velu2X_and_vcYInv_velu2Y_toricPoint_tateLaurent_map_qExpand_eq_toricPoint_sq.lean

